/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch33_fast_intermediate_reduced -- the REDUCED twin of
  batch32_fast_intermediate_full.

  THE REDUCTION.  When I is consumed much faster than it is made, its two
  rates balance, k1 n_A = k2 n_I, and P is made at the rate A is used:

      dn_P/dt = k1 n_A

  This case runs that one law, A -> P, written as an `expression` law in
  constant/reactions.  compB (the intermediate) stays declared and stays at
  zero: the reduced model does not carry it.

  WHAT IS KEPT.  One rate constant, k1, and the two stable species.  k2
  does not appear: it only decides how little I there is, never how fast P
  is made.  What is lost is the I in transit, which batch32 measures.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        batchReactor;

        operation
        {
            mode         isothermal;
            T_setpoint   350.0 K;
        }

        reactions  ( A_to_P );
    }
);
